# /boot/firmware/demiurge.conf
#
# DEMIURGE boot config — a pointer to the file you actually edit.
# Mount the SD card's boot partition on any computer to change this,
# then reboot the Pi. For everything else, edit ~/demiurge/live.conf
# over SSH while the Pi is running (the launcher hot-reloads it).
#
# `launch =` resolves in this order:
#   1. whatever absolute path is set below, if any
#   2. otherwise ~/demiurge/live.conf
#
# Only one user-facing config format exists: live.conf. The simple
# `chain =` interface compiles down to the internal Rust session graph
# at runtime — most users never need to touch the launcher source.
# If you want to point at an alternate live.conf (e.g. a different
# show file), set its absolute path below.

# By default DEMIURGE loads ~/demiurge/live.conf for whoever the launcher
# runs as — no username needed here. Only set an absolute path below if you
# want to point at a DIFFERENT live.conf (e.g. an alternate show file):
# launch = /home/youruser/demiurge/live.conf

# Note: link / bpm / chain / midi all live in ~/demiurge/live.conf,
# not here — they need to be hot-toggleable on save, which only the
# live.conf watcher provides.
